    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d43">

                <pb facs="0051" n="45" sameAs="frus:frus1942v02/pg45"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 European War 1939/19690: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Finland</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Schoenfeld</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Helsinki</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-02-24T14:00:00+02:00">February 24,
                            1942—2 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 4:46 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>144. There has been no reference in Finnish press thus far to Stalin’s
                    declaration yesterday<anchor n="59" xml:id="d43-f1"/> on anniversary of Red Army
                    including his statement that recovery of Baltic States and Karelia is Soviet war
                    aim.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Schoenfeld</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d43-f1" n="59" xml:id="d43-f1-content">
                <p>The Department received a report of Stalin’s speech in telegram No. 163 of
                    February 24, from the Chargé in the Soviet Union, <ref
                        target="frus1942v03#pg_416">vol. <hi rendition="#small-caps">iii</hi>, p.
                        416</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
